<block><txt break.before="1">An Act to provide for the appointment of a Crown
Advocate and to define the duties and functions of the Crown
Advocate.</txt></block></tier>
</content>


<content type="body">

<level type="clause" id="sec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_3adffa73-e8ff-453e-bd04-34a17374fb9c"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>1</no><heading guid="_f7b36d6f-60e7-4342-889c-3bd3cfc7b83c"
id="sec.1-he"><b>Name of Act</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This Act may be cited as the <legref
refid="act-1979-059" jurisd="NSW" type="act" check="unknown"><name
emphasis="yes"><i>Crown Advocate Act
1979</i></name></legref>.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_fa538b33-6a01-4fb2-a64b-3fe377649010"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>2</no><heading guid="_f34c6617-4119-4457-a91b-58562c3789e4"
id="sec.2-he"><b>Definition</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">In this Act, except in so far as the context or
subject-matter otherwise indicates or requires, <defterm type="definition"
guid="_a214adbc-79d6-4f69-ba64-780ccfcb1c49"
id="def.CrownAdvocate"><b><i>Crown Advocate</i></b></defterm> includes the
deputy appointed to act for the Crown Advocate during the Crown
Advocate&#8217;s illness or absence from office.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_15a63b62-3c5c-4377-8aa8-7e64a667f416"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>3</no><heading guid="_d10f060f-6b12-4047-8186-02e9a5b62f7e"
id="sec.3-he"><b>Appointment of Crown Advocate</b></heading></head>

<pre type="auto-inserted">

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.3-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_df993e6d-3c89-44b0-9a15-b13b12a700cf"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Governor may appoint as Crown Advocate an
Australian legal practitioner of at least 7 years&#8217;
standing.</txt></block></tier>
</pre>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.3-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_48ee9649-7ed4-45fd-8855-44ca2397a390"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Any appointment pursuant to subsection (1) may be
on such terms and conditions as the Governor determines.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.3-ssec.3" status="repealed">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_feb3099a-ebe8-4959-a129-5542a0c8ab0c"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3-ssec.3"></attrib>
<attrib name="status" value="repealed"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<repealed><repealedtxt></repealedtxt></repealed>
</tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.3-ssec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_28fe9bec-ded1-439c-882b-dd9001f882f4"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3-ssec.4"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(4)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The office of Crown Advocate shall not be held by
a Minister of the Crown.</txt></block></tier>


<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 3:</b> Am 1990 No 99,
Sch 4; 1993 No 87, Sch 5; 2008 No 62, Sch 3.2.</txt></content>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_3ba022db-8c1b-48d7-b51d-d4b27e5ce080"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>4</no><heading guid="_d7de3c00-e2b0-4248-9372-93f824e13ea5"
id="sec.4-he"><b><legref refid="act-2013-040" jurisd="NSW" type="act"
check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Government Sector Employment Act
2013</i></name></legref> not to apply</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The office of Crown Advocate is a statutory
office and the <legref refid="act-2013-040" jurisd="NSW" type="act"
check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Government Sector Employment Act
2013</i></name></legref> does not apply to that office.</txt></block>

<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 4:</b> Subst 2015 No
15, Sch 3.18.</txt></content>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.5">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_4c9c5206-5d69-4c8c-b8dc-2262d4d74d81"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>5</no><heading guid="_0d219e2c-d56f-44ec-b585-b3d8b79d3b6c"
id="sec.5-he"><b>Term of office</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.5-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_d3e5da6f-4773-44cf-b9db-779d9a5d71ae"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Subject to this Act, the Crown Advocate shall
hold office for such term, not exceeding 7 years, as is specified in the
instrument of his or her appointment.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.5-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_fa0481f8-f78f-4958-a34e-abd9e4e28f39"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Crown Advocate shall, if otherwise qualified,
be eligible for re-appointment from time to time for such term, not exceeding
7 years, as is specified in the instrument of his or her
re-appointment.</txt></block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.6">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_09fc0028-d4e7-4535-8b0b-916dfa0d0932"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>6</no><heading guid="_14b072a5-fbb7-4d5c-b991-020f580d6cf2"
id="sec.6-he"><b>Vacation of office</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_c8097770-1330-45b7-b54f-3c23859fd720"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Crown Advocate shall be deemed to have
vacated the office of Crown Advocate:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_ba414b2f-9ed7-4263-a9f7-33bddf6bdfea" id="sec.6-ssec.1-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">if the Crown Advocate is removed from office by
the Governor pursuant to subsection (2),</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_6c30aa07-d7df-4166-8a50-e7cbbb39b6c7" id="sec.6-ssec.1-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">if the Crown Advocate becomes bankrupt, applies
to take the benefit of any law for the relief of bankrupt or insolvent
debtors, compounds with his or her creditors or makes an assignment of his or
her remuneration, allowances or estate for their benefit,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_a397a30b-57df-4baa-a5f9-ae694d970916" id="sec.6-ssec.1-para1.c">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">if the Crown Advocate becomes a temporary
patient, a continued treatment patient, a protected person or an incapable
person within the meaning of the <legref jurisd="NSW" type="act"
check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Mental Health Act
1958</i></name></legref> or a person under detention under Part 7 of that
Act,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_7afa7a52-a08c-4acd-9198-9f9228f87d06" id="sec.6-ssec.1-para1.d">
<no>(d)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">if the Crown Advocate resigns the office by
instrument in writing addressed to the Governor, or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_563e4af1-aaa4-4016-8c0e-a2fb2c5e2716" id="sec.6-ssec.1-para1.e"
status="repealed">
<no>(e)</no>
<repealed><repealedtxt></repealedtxt></repealed>
</li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_28f5c722-3639-4ed1-b248-2ed4f7a1c9e8" id="sec.6-ssec.1-para1.f">
<no>(f)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">if the Crown Advocate engages (whether in New
South Wales or elsewhere) during the Crown Advocate&#8217;s term of office in
any paid employment or in any remunerated practice of law outside the duties
of the office.</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_4c3e70d7-31ab-4f36-b64b-31bb49ff327b" id="sec.6-ssec.1-para1.g"
status="repealed">
<no>(g)</no>
<repealed><repealedtxt></repealedtxt></repealed>
</li></list>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_7f347dbd-b504-4995-ade3-0d4634039197"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Governor may, for any cause which appears to
the Governor to be sufficient, remove the Crown Advocate from
office.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6-ssec.3" status="repealed">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_2ad8acfd-cc64-4f10-a42f-70488a9f2e1f"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6-ssec.3"></attrib>
<attrib name="status" value="repealed"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<repealed><repealedtxt></repealedtxt></repealed>
</tier>


<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 6:</b> Am 1980 No 187,
Sch 1; 1990 No 44, sec 4; 1990 No 99, Sch 4.</txt></content>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.7">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_c76dcd12-ec1b-4cb8-8e86-d8d101f2b0be"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>7</no><heading guid="_c8d75b92-f5ef-48fa-bf0e-fff2dbd611b3"
id="sec.7-he"><b>Remuneration and leave</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_61267d73-a290-4f05-9937-1cd318526c18"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Crown Advocate is entitled to be paid:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_75aa7843-9f06-4b47-8ad8-1e6201dd65e9" id="sec.7-ssec.1-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">remuneration in accordance with the <legref
refid="act-1976-004" jurisd="NSW" type="act" check="unknown"><name
emphasis="yes"><i>Statutory and Other Offices Remuneration Act
1975</i></name></legref>, and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_12346a84-1f48-48bb-a9ac-6838f41b606b" id="sec.7-ssec.1-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">such travelling and subsistence allowances as the
Minister may from time to time determine in respect of the Crown
Advocate.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_1ea51403-bf2f-4701-b98c-d0f6e02d3a5e"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The leave which may be granted to the Crown
Advocate shall be as the Minister may from time to time determine in respect
of the Crown Advocate.</txt></block></tier>


<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 7:</b> Am 1987 No 48,
Sch 30.</txt></content>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.8">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_ce0fbbb5-7b53-4949-9b78-70f6e6d1f426"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.8"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>8</no><heading guid="_527b8f09-5d20-4ce6-98aa-d2d530dc4dca"
id="sec.8-he"><b>Deputy of Crown Advocate during Crown Advocate&#8217;s
illness or absence</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.8-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_be4b0764-8627-4e97-86a2-7777540b5693"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.8-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">In the case of the illness or absence from office
of the Crown Advocate, the Governor may appoint a deputy to act for the Crown
Advocate during the Crown Advocate&#8217;s illness or
absence.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.8-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_2a5162ef-3cea-4eb4-bb58-f68b6161ce48"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.8-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Without affecting the generality of subsection
(1), the Crown Advocate is, for the purposes of that subsection, absent from
the office of Crown Advocate during any period that the Crown Advocate is
appointed to act for the Solicitor General under section 2 (1) of the <legref
refid="act-1969-080" jurisd="NSW" type="act" check="unknown"><name
emphasis="yes"><i>Solicitor General Act
1969</i></name></legref>.</txt></block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.9">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_dad4704b-7595-45a6-930b-76566b0cc435"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.9"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>9</no><heading guid="_87d45ef8-e23c-4b49-b28f-8af25f44ba66"
id="sec.9-he"><b>Duties and functions of Crown Advocate</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The duties and functions of the Crown Advocate
are:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_9339608d-f0cc-482f-ba65-90049ff73470" id="sec.9-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">to assist the Solicitor General in respect of the
exercise or discharge by the Solicitor General of any powers, authorities,
duties or functions delegated by the Attorney General under section 4 of the
<legref refid="act-1969-080" jurisd="NSW" type="act" check="unknown"><name
emphasis="yes"><i>Solicitor General Act 1969</i></name></legref>,
and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_bf40cd38-8447-4b58-9c25-afc1ae723c0f" id="sec.9-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">to advise and conduct proceedings on behalf of
the Director of Public Prosecutions, with the consent of the Attorney General
and at the request of the Director, and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_d8b97015-612d-48b2-8fa8-5e23a636a753" id="sec.9-para1.c">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">whenever directed by the Attorney General, to act
as counsel for the Crown in right of the State, for the Attorney General or
for any other person in any criminal or civil proceedings or in any inquiry or
commission, and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_0a3ef133-c3d9-45c2-89f1-0ae18d64d1df" id="sec.9-para1.d">
<no>(d)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">to advise the Attorney General in respect of any
matter referred to the Crown Advocate by the Attorney General,
and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_f2b8b1b1-d8b7-4242-b055-edc468167fa9" id="sec.9-para1.e">
<no>(e)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">to carry out such other duties and functions of
counsel as the Attorney General directs, and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_3880fbe3-149b-4444-aed6-0a4326e651a5" id="sec.9-para1.f">
<no>(f)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">to carry out other duties and functions conferred
or imposed on the Crown Advocate by or under this or any other
Act.</txt></block></li></list>
</block>

<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 9:</b> Am 1986 No 212,
Sch 1; 1998 No 49, Sch 8 [1] [2].</txt></content>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.10">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_b5112a7f-0d1b-4321-b8a0-f1c5fb39f62c"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.10"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>10</no><heading guid="_db4b1685-24b1-4deb-9b59-e848b2cef4b1"
id="sec.10-he"><b>Delegation of functions by Attorney
General</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.10-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_7c294e50-566b-435b-b199-2311147ca139"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.10-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Attorney General may, by instrument in
writing, delegate to the Crown Advocate the exercise or discharge of such of
the powers (other than this power of delegation), authorities, duties and
functions that may be exercised or discharged by the Attorney General and as
may be specified in the instrument of delegation, and may in like manner
revoke wholly or in part any such delegation.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.10-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_dfd75ef0-eb79-425c-b2a4-8941673627c3"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.10-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">A delegation made under this section may be made
subject to such conditions or such limitations as to the exercise or discharge
of any of the specified powers, authorities, duties or functions delegated or
as to time or circumstances as may be specified in the instrument of
delegation.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.10-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_9b3300a7-b499-4353-b2d4-fbf8ed132a92"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.10-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Notwithstanding any delegation made under this
section, the Attorney General may continue to exercise or discharge all or any
of the powers, authorities, duties or functions
delegated.</txt></block></tier>


<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 10:</b> Ins 1998 No 49,
Sch 8 [3].</txt></content>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.11">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_1636164f-ed26-4535-925e-ba751be6f2ce"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.11"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>11</no><heading guid="_c4d14e12-e8de-494b-b3e1-ac22e2d8857e"
id="sec.11-he"><b>Exercise of delegated functions</b></heading></head>

<pre type="auto-inserted">

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.11-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_6328231a-eebc-4585-9254-3c23bf4e4de2"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.11-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Any power, authority, duty or function, the
exercise or discharge of which has been delegated under section 10, may, while
the delegation remains unrevoked, be exercised or discharged in accordance
with the terms of the delegation by the Crown Advocate.</txt></block></tier>
</pre>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.11-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_b373a94b-fc5e-42bf-b98b-f832a2ffa9b6"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.11-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Any act or thing done or suffered by the Crown
Advocate, when acting in the exercise of a delegation made under section 10
and within the terms of the delegation, has the like force and effect as if
the act or thing had been done or suffered by the Attorney
General.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.11-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_0f7d3df6-80f5-412b-a53f-d55048258aaa"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.11-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Where any power, authority, duty or function is
exercised or discharged under a delegation made under section 10, and its
exercise or discharge depends on the opinion, belief or state of mind of the
Attorney General, that power, authority, duty or function may be exercised or
discharged by the Crown Advocate on the opinion, belief or state of mind of
the Crown Advocate.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.11-ssec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_7e2a7b60-5a55-4526-8f37-c79c14223675"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.11-ssec.4"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(4)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">No person is to be concerned to see or inquire
into whether any act, matter or thing done or performed by the Crown Advocate
when purporting to act under a delegation made under section 10 is or is not
authorised by that delegation.</txt></block></tier>


<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 11:</b> Ins 1998 No 49,
Sch 8 [3].</txt></content>
</level>
</content>


